STEP BY STEP (THE NARRATIVE)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa51\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \
1. The High Elvis is about to go on for his own set (post-platform, post-Eloise\'92s arrival \'97 those beats belong to Scene 2 and have already happened; do not restage them) when the three active Sages \'97 Kleo, Chilo, Solo, the only three of the original Seven still active (kleo.md: \'93only three of the seven still active\'94) \'97 appear on stage unannounced and unplanned, carrying ukuleles.\
2. Kleo addresses the High Elvis directly, verbatim: \'93Just a little public service announcement.\'94 the High Elvis waves them through \'97 no alarm, no hesitation, procedural calm.\
3. The Sages play the ditty once through, straight, no elaboration or introduction \'97 verbatim, do not alter a word: \'93Praise the Dawkins / He\'92s the One / Praise the Dawkins / And the One after the One / The Holy Momma / And her unborn Son / Praise the Dawkins / To Kingdom Come.\'94\
4. They pivot into a call-and-response game with the crowd (~half a million on the lawn plus the live stream \'97 established-facts.md \'a7Rock Against Revival), escalating in this order: back of the crowd, then front; then just the Elvi; then the Cloudborne; a beat of surprise at the volume (\'93wow, that was loud\'94); then a challenge \'97 can the Airborne kids outdo the Cloudborne kids.\
5. Kleo takes a ukulele lead break: \'93full of hammers and pulls that would make a Los Angeles Guitar Academy graduate proud, but left this audience wondering why stringed instruments were ever invented in the first place.\'94 Play this for bathos, not triumph \'97 technically virtuosic, tonally baffling, not delightful.\
6. Named reactions: the Holy Momma (Sarah), Aunt Kathy and Aunt Hayley react in shock. Eloise \'93laughs so hard, such as she has not laughed so honestly in decades,\'94 and delivers the closing line verbatim: \'93Oh sweet Holy spreadsheets, these guys are good for business.\'94\
7. Scene ends there. No thesis statement, no victory lap for the Sages, no further payoff \'97 this is their entire presence in the Rock Against Revival sequence.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa51\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs26 \cf2 WHOSE EYES, AND THE TONE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa51\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs22 \cf2 \
\'95 POV needs a vantage that holds the stage action and the four named platform reactions in one frame \'97 plausibly Sarah or Eloise\'92s close-third, since the platform (established in Scene 2) is the only place that has Sarah, Kathy, Hayley and Eloise together.\
\'95 Tone: pure bathos. Kleo\'92s PSA line and the High Elvis\'92s wave-through should read as bureaucratic and unhurried \'97 an interruption absorbed with total institutional calm \'97 set against the audacity of the ditty\'92s content (a mock-liturgy about \'93the Holy Momma / And her unborn Son\'94 sung by half a million strangers who mostly don\'92t know or care what it means). Comedy comes from the mismatch of scale and stakes, not from menace.\
\'95 Kleo\'92s line should land in his established voice: whisper/raspy register, elaborate bureaucratic-mystical courtesy (kleo.md: \'93Excuse me, dear lady\'94; \'93this is facilitative oversight, it\'92s our job\'94) \'97 faux-modest, procedural, not sly or scheming.\
\'95 Chilo and Solo are present as the other two ukuleles (three Sages, three instruments) but the brief gives no individual dialogue for either \'97 do not invent lines for them. Stage them physically per their own established costume/business (chilo.md, solo.md) but keep them silent/backing figures; all spoken lines in this scene belong to Kleo.\
\'95 The reaction beat is a reaction shot, not a debate \'97 don\'92t let Sarah, Kathy or Hayley argue theology on the page here. Play \'93shock\'94 through each one\'92s own established idiom rather than a generic gasp: Kathy tends physical/exclamatory, Hayley tends flat and dry (understated shock, not a gasp), Sarah tends contained \'97 her hand drifting to her belly before she can stop it is her established tell for exposure/discomfort (content.rtf, Inauguration scene precedent, verified verbatim: \'93Sarah\'92s hand drifted to her belly before she could stop it\'94) and is the natural instinct to reach for here rather than inventing a new gesture.\
\'95 Eloise\'92s laugh is the tonal keystone and should land last, as the closing beat \'97 it reframes everything before it as good marketing rather than heresy, and is funnier for coming after three people react as though something sacred has been violated.\
